  "body": {
    "id": "thm:fixed-budget-greedy-guarantee",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "For every \\((p,k,m,M,s,V)\\in\\mathfrak T\\) and every \\(P\\in\\mathcal M_{p,k}(m,M,s,V)\\), let \\(\\rho_k(K,R)\\) be the exact frontier at \\(K=M/m\\) and \\(R=V/s\\).  Population forward greedy satisfies\n\\[\n F(S_g)\\ge\\left\\{1-\\left(1-\\frac{\\rho_k(K,R)}{k}\\right)^k\\right\\}\\mathrm{OPT}\n \\ge\\{1-e^{-\\rho_k(K,R)}\\}\\mathrm{OPT}.\n\\]\nOn the event \\(\\max_{|S|\\le k}|\\widehat B(S)-B(S)|\\le\\epsilon\\), empirical forward greedy satisfies\n\\[\n F(\\widehat S)\\ge\n \\left\\{1-\\left(1-\\frac{\\rho_k(K,R)}{k}\\right)^k\\right\\}\\mathrm{OPT}-4k\\epsilon.\n\\]\nThus, for \\(k\\ge2\\) and \\(R>1\\), the factor uses \\(\\rho_k(K,R)=k/\\{1+(k-1)KR\\}\\); for \\(k=1\\) or \\(R=1\\), it uses \\(\\rho_k(K,R)=1\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
